The TLS stack has no wasm32 target.

`rustls` is pinned to its `ring` provider, and `ring` builds its assembly and C
through a build script that has no wasm32-wasip2 path — so the cross-build fails
in the dependency, before reaching any of this package's own code.

This is not a defect in `server`, and it is not fixable here by target-gating:
TLS is the point of the package rather than an optional device, so there is no
useful build with it cfg'd out (unlike graphics, whose window layer is separable
from its canvas — see loft's WASM.md § When the crate needs a device the target
does not have).

Delete this file when `rustls` can be built for wasm32 here — most likely by
moving off the `ring` provider — and the gate will hold the package to it.
